IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tda-common`
IMPORT `fhog-terms`
IMPORT `tda-transfer`
IMPORT `tda-vehicles`
IMPORT `fhog-grant`

-- Duties Act 2001 and First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (Tas) -- the buyer's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the buyer -- the transferee of a home (a first home buyer, or a pensioner who is downsizing), the applicant for
-- the first home owner grant, and the person who applies to register a motor vehicle. Every question is phrased as that
-- person would ask it, on facts that person could state. The rules are in tda-transfer.l4, tda-vehicles.l4,
-- fhog-grant.l4, fhog-terms.l4 and tda-common.l4; this module builds their records from plain answers and restates no
-- rule. The Commissioner of State Revenue is a party to the rules, never a seat.
--
-- THE SEAT'S REACH: one buyer, or one buyer and one other individual (plus the Commonwealth or Housing Australia under
-- Help to Buy); the buyer asking is the pensioner in the pensioner questions. The core takes any number of transferees.
-- The figures are the deposited text's: the eligible periods end on 30 June 2026 (s 57C), 30 June 2024 (s 46A) and
-- 30 June 2025 (s 46J), and the caps are $750 000 and $600 000; the Division 2C period, which sets the reach of that
-- unencoded concession, ends on 30 June 2026 (s 46S). A Minister's extension order (ss 46B, 46K, 46T, 57D) or a
-- prescribed amount (Duties Regulations 2021, not deposited) would change the answers (NOTES.md). The Division 2A and 2B
-- caps are known only from 1 January 2022: an earlier transfer whose answer turns on them is `not covered` (the core).
--
-- Where a judgment is the Commissioner's, the question asks it conditionally: "... (the Commissioner must also be of
-- that opinion)".
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Buying a home, and registering a vehicle, in Tasmania -- the buyer's questions`

§§ `Building the core's records from my answers`

GIVEN `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the building is suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Building facts`
`the building from my answers` `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` `the building is suitable to live in` `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since` MEANS
    `Building facts` WITH
        `is a building affixed to land`                                               IS `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in`
        `may lawfully be used as a place of residence`                                IS `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in`
        `is, in the Commissioner's opinion, suitable for use as a place of residence` IS `the building is suitable to live in`
        `has previously been occupied or sold as a place of residence`                IS `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before`
        `would be new residential premises because of substantial renovations (GST Act s 40-75(1)(b))` IS `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since`
        -- the second limb of s 3 "new home" (b)(ii) is folded into the one answer above
        `has been occupied or sold as a place of residence since those renovations`   IS FALSE

-- One individual buyer, for the first home buyer tests. The Division 2B fields are filled in separately for the buyer
-- asking (`me as the buyer`); for another buyer they are a fixed FALSE, as the seat asks the pensioner questions of the
-- buyer asking only.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `exempted from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `owned a home before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid a grant before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `had the concession before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `had the exemption before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `intends to live there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Transferee`
`an individual buyer` `age` `exempted from the age requirement` `citizen or permanent resident` `owned a home before` `paid a grant before` `had the concession before` `had the exemption before` `intends to live there` MEANS
    `Transferee` WITH
        `is the Commonwealth or Housing Australia under a Help to Buy arrangement`                          IS FALSE
        `is a natural person`                                                                              IS TRUE
        `age at the transfer`                                                                              IS `age`
        `the Commissioner exempts the age requirement (ss 46C(2), 57E(2))`                                 IS `exempted from the age requirement`
        `is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident`                                                 IS `citizen or permanent resident`
        `the person or spouse has previously been the owner of a home in Tasmania or any other State or a Territory` IS `owned a home before`
        `the person or spouse has previously been paid a first home owner grant under the FHOG Act 2000`   IS `paid a grant before`
        `a previous transfer to the person or spouse attracted a Division 2A concession`                   IS `had the concession before`
        `no duty was charged on a previous transfer to the person or spouse under Part 6 Division 2`       IS `had the exemption before`
        `intends to meet the residence requirement`                                                        IS `intends to live there`
        `holds a Pensioner Concession Card under a relevant Act of the Commonwealth`                       IS FALSE
        `holds a Seniors Health Card (Social Security Act 1991)`                                           IS FALSE
        `receives a special rate pension (Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986)`                                IS FALSE
        `a previous transfer to the person or spouse attracted a Division 2B concession`                   IS FALSE

GIVEN `b` IS A `Transferee`
      `card` IS A BOOLEAN, `seniors card` IS A BOOLEAN, `pension` IS A BOOLEAN, `had it before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Transferee`
`with the pensioner facts` `b` `card` `seniors card` `pension` `had it before` MEANS
    `Transferee` WITH
        `is the Commonwealth or Housing Australia under a Help to Buy arrangement`                          IS `b`'s `is the Commonwealth or Housing Australia under a Help to Buy arrangement`
        `is a natural person`                                                                              IS `b`'s `is a natural person`
        `age at the transfer`                                                                              IS `b`'s `age at the transfer`
        `the Commissioner exempts the age requirement (ss 46C(2), 57E(2))`                                 IS `b`'s `the Commissioner exempts the age requirement (ss 46C(2), 57E(2))`
        `is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident`                                                 IS `b`'s `is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident`
        `the person or spouse has previously been the owner of a home in Tasmania or any other State or a Territory` IS `b`'s `the person or spouse has previously been the owner of a home in Tasmania or any other State or a Territory`
        `the person or spouse has previously been paid a first home owner grant under the FHOG Act 2000`   IS `b`'s `the person or spouse has previously been paid a first home owner grant under the FHOG Act 2000`
        `a previous transfer to the person or spouse attracted a Division 2A concession`                   IS `b`'s `a previous transfer to the person or spouse attracted a Division 2A concession`
        `no duty was charged on a previous transfer to the person or spouse under Part 6 Division 2`       IS `b`'s `no duty was charged on a previous transfer to the person or spouse under Part 6 Division 2`
        `intends to meet the residence requirement`                                                        IS `b`'s `intends to meet the residence requirement`
        `holds a Pensioner Concession Card under a relevant Act of the Commonwealth`                       IS `card`
        `holds a Seniors Health Card (Social Security Act 1991)`                                           IS `seniors card`
        `receives a special rate pension (Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986)`                                IS `pension`
        `a previous transfer to the person or spouse attracted a Division 2B concession`                   IS `had it before`

-- The Commonwealth or Housing Australia as a co-transferee under Help to Buy. s 32 leaves it out of every test, so its
-- other fields are never read: fixed placeholders.
`Housing Australia under Help to Buy` MEANS
    `Transferee` WITH
        `is the Commonwealth or Housing Australia under a Help to Buy arrangement`                          IS TRUE
        `is a natural person`                                                                              IS FALSE
        `age at the transfer`                                                                              IS 0
        `the Commissioner exempts the age requirement (ss 46C(2), 57E(2))`                                 IS FALSE
        `is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident`                                                 IS FALSE
        `the person or spouse has previously been the owner of a home in Tasmania or any other State or a Territory` IS FALSE
        `the person or spouse has previously been paid a first home owner grant under the FHOG Act 2000`   IS FALSE
        `a previous transfer to the person or spouse attracted a Division 2A concession`                   IS FALSE
        `no duty was charged on a previous transfer to the person or spouse under Part 6 Division 2`       IS FALSE
        `intends to meet the residence requirement`                                                        IS FALSE
        `holds a Pensioner Concession Card under a relevant Act of the Commonwealth`                       IS FALSE
        `holds a Seniors Health Card (Social Security Act 1991)`                                           IS FALSE
        `receives a special rate pension (Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986)`                                IS FALSE
        `a previous transfer to the person or spouse attracted a Division 2B concession`                   IS FALSE

GIVEN `me` IS A `Transferee`, `with another` IS A BOOLEAN, `the other` IS A `Transferee`, `help to buy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Transferee`
`the transferees from my answers` `me` `with another` `the other` `help to buy` MEANS
    IF `with another`
    THEN IF `help to buy`
         THEN LIST `me`, `the other`, `Housing Australia under Help to Buy`
         ELSE LIST `me`, `the other`
    ELSE IF `help to buy`
         THEN LIST `me`, `Housing Australia under Help to Buy`
         ELSE LIST `me`

-- A pensioner with no former home: the s 46N/46O facts are never reached. Fixed placeholders.
`no former home` MEANS
    `Former home` WITH
        `the pensioner has a former home in Tasmania that they lived in as principal place of residence`  IS FALSE
        `the day it was or will be transferred`                                                         IS YearMonthDay 2000 1 1
        `its dutiable value when transferred`                                                           IS 0
        `it was the principal place of residence for the 6 months before it was transferred (or a lesser period approved)` IS FALSE
        `it was the principal place of residence for the 6 months before the new purchase (or a lesser period approved)`  IS FALSE
        `the new home is in the same name or names as the former home, or the Commissioner is satisfied of good reasons`  IS FALSE
        `the pensioner or spouse owned another home (not the former or new home) at the time of the purchase`             IS FALSE

GIVEN `selling` IS A BOOLEAN, `sold on` IS A DATE, `worth` IS A NUMBER, `lived before selling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `lived before buying` IS A BOOLEAN, `same names` IS A BOOLEAN, `another home` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Former home`
`the former home from my answers` `selling` `sold on` `worth` `lived before selling` `lived before buying` `same names` `another home` MEANS
    `Former home` WITH
        `the pensioner has a former home in Tasmania that they lived in as principal place of residence`  IS `selling`
        `the day it was or will be transferred`                                                         IS `sold on`
        `its dutiable value when transferred`                                                           IS `worth`
        `it was the principal place of residence for the 6 months before it was transferred (or a lesser period approved)` IS `lived before selling`
        `it was the principal place of residence for the 6 months before the new purchase (or a lesser period approved)`  IS `lived before buying`
        `the new home is in the same name or names as the former home, or the Commissioner is satisfied of good reasons`  IS `same names`
        `the pensioner or spouse owned another home (not the former or new home) at the time of the purchase`             IS `another home`

GIVEN `day` IS A DATE, `price` IS A NUMBER, `value` IS A NUMBER, `building on land` IS A BOOLEAN, `building` IS A `Building facts`
      `buyers` IS A LIST OF `Transferee`
      `former` IS A `Former home`, `good reasons` IS A BOOLEAN, `foreign corporation or trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `off the plan` IS A BOOLEAN, `agreement day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Home transfer`
`the transfer from my answers` `day` `price` `value` `building on land` `building` `buyers` `former` `good reasons` `foreign corporation or trustee` `off the plan` `agreement day` MEANS
    `Home transfer` WITH
        `the day of the transfer`                                                                          IS `day`
        `the consideration`                                                                                IS `price`
        `the unencumbered value`                                                                           IS `value`
        `the land has a building on it`                                                                    IS `building on land`
        `the building`                                                                                     IS `building`
        `the transferees`                                                                                  IS `buyers`
        `the former home`                                                                                  IS `former`
        `the Commissioner is satisfied there are good reasons why a transferee is not an eligible first home buyer` IS `good reasons`
        -- only the ss 13-15 rule reads this; the duty questions do not
        `is effected by a written instrument`                                                              IS TRUE
        `a transferee is a foreign corporation or a foreign trustee`                                       IS `foreign corporation or trustee`
        `is of a strata or conjoined dwelling with no occupancy permit granted when the agreement for sale was executed` IS `off the plan`
        `the day the agreement for sale was executed`                                                      IS `agreement day`

§§ `The dutiable value and the general rate (ss 18-20, 29)`

@export What is the dutiable value of my Tasmanian home purchase: the greater of the price and the property's value (Duties Act 2001 s 18)?
GIVEN `the price I pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you pay for the land and home, in Australian dollars, including any debt or mortgage you take over; under Help to Buy, the full price including the Commonwealth's contribution
      `what the property was worth when I signed the contract` IS A NUMBER @desc What the property could reasonably have been sold for on the open market when the contract was signed, free of any mortgage, in dollars, leaving out improvements you made yourself before the transfer
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the dutiable value of my home` IS
    `the dutiable value (s 18(1))` `the price I pay` `what the property was worth when I signed the contract`

@export How much transfer duty is charged at the general rate on a Tasmanian property with this dutiable value (Duties Act 2001 s 29, $50 to $4.50 per $100 or part)?
GIVEN `the dutiable value` IS A NUMBER @desc The dutiable value of the property, in Australian dollars (the greater of the price and the property's market value)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the duty at the general rate` IS
    `the duty at the s 29 general rate on` `the dutiable value`

@export We are buying as joint tenants: what share of the property is each of us taken to hold when the duty is assessed (Duties Act 2001 s 12)?
GIVEN `how many of us are joint tenants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are buying the property together as joint tenants
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What share does each joint tenant hold for duty` IS
    `the share of each joint tenant (s 12)` `how many of us are joint tenants`

§§ `New or established home: the duty exemption or the grant`

@export Is the home I am buying a new home or an established home, and so which can help me: the first home buyer duty exemption or the first home owner grant (FHOG Act ss 3, 4; Duties Act s 57C)?
GIVEN `there is a building on the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a building on the land you are buying (answer no for vacant land you will build on)
      `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be used as a place of residence
      `the building is suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is suitable to live in (the Commissioner of State Revenue must also be of that opinion)
      `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone has lived in the home, or it has been sold as a place of residence, before your purchase
      `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home was substantially renovated so that it counts as new residential premises for GST, and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since the renovations
GIVETH A `Which relief can apply`
DECIDE `Which relief can apply to my home` IS
    `which relief the land can open (Duties Act s 57F(1); FHOG Act s 13(1))` `there is a building on the land`
        (`the building from my answers` `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` `the building is suitable to live in` `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since`)

@export Did this interest in land make me (or does it make me) an owner of a home, for the first home owner grant and the duty exemption (FHOG Act ss 3, 5)?
GIVEN `the kind of interest` IS A `Kind of interest` @desc The kind of interest held: fee simple (ordinary freehold), a life estate, a perpetual lease or convertible leasehold from the Commonwealth or the State, an instalment purchase from the Commonwealth or the State, a Crown licence or right of occupancy, company shares giving exclusive occupation of a home, a Help to Buy interest of the Commonwealth or Housing Australia, or another interest
      `the Commissioner approved or accepted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a life estate, a Crown licence or company shares only: whether the Commissioner approved the life estate, is of the opinion the licence gives reasonable security, or is satisfied about the shares
      `it gave a right to live there within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the interest gave, or would within 12 months (or a longer time the Commissioner allowed) give, a right to immediate occupation of the land
      `it was held subject to a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person held the interest subject to a trust (for example, as trustee)
      `it was an equitable interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the interest was only an equitable interest (for example, under an unregistered arrangement)
      `a guardian held it on trust for a person under a legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a guardian held the interest on trust for a person under a legal disability
      `the Commissioner recognised it anyway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner recognised the interest as a relevant interest even though it does not fit the usual kinds (s 5(4))
      `there was a building on the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there was a building on the land
      `the building was fixed to the land and could lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building was fixed to the land and could lawfully be used as a place of residence
      `the building was suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building was suitable to live in (the Commissioner must also be of that opinion)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this interest make me an owner of a home` IF
    `makes the holder an owner of a home (FHOG Act ss 3, 5(1))`
        (`Interest facts` WITH
            `kind`                                                                         IS `the kind of interest`
            `the Commissioner approves it, or is of the opinion or satisfied that s 5(2) requires` IS `the Commissioner approved or accepted it`
            `gives a right to immediate occupation now or within 12 months (or a longer time allowed)` IS `it gave a right to live there within 12 months`
            `is held subject to a trust`                                                   IS `it was held subject to a trust`
            `is an equitable interest`                                                     IS `it was an equitable interest`
            `is held on trust by a guardian for a person under a legal disability`         IS `a guardian held it on trust for a person under a legal disability`
            `the Commissioner recognises it as a non-conforming interest (s 5(4))`         IS `the Commissioner recognised it anyway`)
        -- ownership reads only s 4 "home": whether the building was lived in before or renovated (s 3 "new home") is not
        -- read, so those two answers are fixed placeholders (TRUE, FALSE)
        (`the building from my answers` `the building was fixed to the land and could lawfully be lived in` `the building was suitable to live in` TRUE FALSE)
        `there was a building on the land`

DECLARE `Spouse answer` HAS
    `my spouse for the first home owner grant (FHOG Act s 6)`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `my spouse for the duty exemption (Duties Act s 3)`          IS A BOOLEAN

@export Does this person count as my spouse -- for the first home owner grant, and for the first home buyer duty exemption (FHOG Act s 6; Duties Act s 3)?
GIVEN `we are legally married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and this person are legally married
      `we are in a significant relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and this person are in a significant relationship within the meaning of the Relationships Act 2003 (Tas)
      `we live apart and do not intend to live together again` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are legally married but not living together, with no intention of resuming (the Commissioner must be satisfied of this)
GIVETH A `Spouse answer`
DECIDE `Does this person count as my spouse` IS
    `Spouse answer` WITH
        `my spouse for the first home owner grant (FHOG Act s 6)`   IS `is a spouse for the grant (FHOG Act s 6)` `the relationship`
        `my spouse for the duty exemption (Duties Act s 3)`          IS `is a spouse for the Duties Act (s 3)` `the relationship`
    WHERE
        `the relationship` MEANS
            `Relationship facts` WITH
                `are legally married`                                            IS `we are legally married`
                `are in a significant relationship (Relationships Act 2003)`     IS `we are in a significant relationship`
                `are not cohabiting, with no intention of resuming cohabitation` IS `we live apart and do not intend to live together again`

§§ `The first home buyer duty exemption and the 2018-2024 concession (Part 6 Division 2; Part 5 Division 2A)`

DECLARE `My first home buyer status` IS ONE OF
    `I am an eligible first home buyer (s 57E)`
    `I am not an eligible first home buyer` HAS `because` IS A `First home buyer bar`

@export Am I an eligible first home buyer for the Tasmanian first home buyer duty exemption (Duties Act 2001 s 57E)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years on the day the land is transferred to you
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are under 18: whether the Commissioner has exempted you from the age requirement (s 57E(2))
      `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, the holder of a permanent visa, or a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa
      `another buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another person buying the home with you is an Australian citizen or permanent resident (answer no if you are buying alone)
      `I or my spouse have owned a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or your spouse (husband, wife or partner in a significant relationship, even if separated), have ever owned a home anywhere in Australia -- held a relevant interest such as freehold in land with a home on it, whether or not you lived there
      `I or my spouse have been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse have ever been paid a first home owner grant under the Tasmanian First Home Owner Grant Act 2000, even if it was paid back
      `I or my spouse got the 2018-2024 half-duty first home buyer concession before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to you or your spouse got the first home buyer duty concession (Duties Act Part 5 Division 2A)
      `I or my spouse got the first home buyer duty exemption before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to you or your spouse was exempt from duty as a first home buyer (Duties Act Part 6 Division 2)
GIVETH A `My first home buyer status`
DECIDE `Am I an eligible first home buyer` IS
    CONSIDER `the bar on` `the first home buyer duty exemption (Part 6 Division 2)` `for` `me` `given` (`I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` OR `another buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`)
    WHEN JUST `b` THEN `I am not an eligible first home buyer` `b`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `I am an eligible first home buyer (s 57E)`
    WHERE
        `me` MEANS `an individual buyer` `my age` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `I or my spouse have owned a home before` `I or my spouse have been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant` `I or my spouse got the 2018-2024 half-duty first home buyer concession before` `I or my spouse got the first home buyer duty exemption before` TRUE

-- The 27 answers asked by both first home buyer questions below, in this order: the transfer (9), me (8), the other
-- buyer (9), the Commissioner's good reasons (1).
@export Is the transfer of my home exempt from duty under the Tasmanian first home buyer duty exemption, so that no duty is charged (Duties Act 2001 Part 6 Division 2, ss 57C-57G; eligible period 18 February 2024 to 30 June 2026 as deposited)?
GIVEN `the day the land is transferred to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the land is transferred to you (usually settlement)
      `the price I pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you pay, in Australian dollars, including any debt or mortgage you take over; under Help to Buy, the full price including the Commonwealth's contribution
      `what the property was worth when I signed the contract` IS A NUMBER @desc What the property could reasonably have been sold for on the open market when the contract was signed, free of any mortgage, in dollars
      `there is a building on the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a building on the land (answer no for vacant land)
      `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be used as a place of residence
      `the building is suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is suitable to live in (the Commissioner must also be of that opinion)
      `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone has lived in the home, or it has been sold as a place of residence, before your purchase (yes for most homes that are not brand new)
      `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home was substantially renovated so that it counts as new residential premises for GST, and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since
      `I am buying under the Help to Buy scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying under a Help to Buy arrangement with Housing Australia (the Commonwealth's share is left out, s 32)
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years on the day of the transfer
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are under 18: whether the Commissioner has exempted you from the age requirement
      `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, the holder of a permanent visa, or a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa
      `I or my spouse have owned a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse (husband, wife or significant-relationship partner, even if separated) have ever owned a home anywhere in Australia, whether or not you lived there
      `I or my spouse have been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse have ever been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant, even if it was paid back
      `I or my spouse got the 2018-2024 half-duty first home buyer concession before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to you or your spouse got the Division 2A first home buyer duty concession
      `I or my spouse got the first home buyer duty exemption before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to you or your spouse was exempt from duty as a first home buyer
      `I intend to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you intend to live in the home as your principal place of residence for at least 6 continuous months, starting within 12 months after the transfer (the Commissioner must be satisfied of this)
      `I am buying with one other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying the home with one other individual (not counting Housing Australia under Help to Buy)
      `the other buyer's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The other buyer's age in years on the day of the transfer
      `the Commissioner has exempted the other buyer from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the other buyer is under 18: whether the Commissioner has exempted them from the age requirement
      `the other buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident
      `the other buyer or their spouse has owned a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other buyer or their spouse has ever owned a home anywhere in Australia
      `the other buyer or their spouse has been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other buyer or their spouse has ever been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant
      `the other buyer or their spouse got the 2018-2024 half-duty concession before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to the other buyer or their spouse got the Division 2A concession
      `the other buyer or their spouse got the first home buyer duty exemption before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to the other buyer or their spouse was exempt as a first home buyer
      `the other buyer intends to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other buyer intends to live in the home as their principal place of residence for 6 continuous months starting within 12 months
      `the Commissioner accepts good reasons why a buyer who is not a first home buyer should not stop the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied there are good reasons why a buyer who is not an eligible first home buyer should not prevent the exemption (s 57F(2)); answer no unless the Commissioner has said so
GIVETH A `First home buyer answer`
DECIDE `Is my home transfer exempt as a first home buyer` IS
    -- the first home buyer test reads neither the former home nor the foreign and Division 2C facts: fixed placeholders
    -- (no former home; FALSE, FALSE and a 1 January 2000 agreement day)
    `the first home buyer test under` `the first home buyer duty exemption (Part 6 Division 2)` `the settings in the deposited text`
        (`the transfer from my answers` `the day the land is transferred to me` `the price I pay` `what the property was worth when I signed the contract` `there is a building on the land` (`the building from my answers` `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` `the building is suitable to live in` `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since`)
