            `no former home` `the Commissioner accepts good reasons why a buyer who is not a first home buyer should not stop the exemption` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1))

@export Did my home purchase, transferred between 7 February 2018 and 30 June 2024, get the half-duty first home buyer duty concession (Duties Act 2001 Part 5 Division 2A, ss 46A-46E; a transfer before 1 January 2022 that turns on the cap is not covered, as the cap then in force is not deposited)?
GIVEN `the day the land is transferred to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the land was transferred to you (usually settlement)
      `the price I pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you paid, in Australian dollars, including any debt or mortgage you took over
      `what the property was worth when I signed the contract` IS A NUMBER @desc What the property could reasonably have been sold for on the open market when the contract was signed, free of any mortgage, in dollars
      `there is a building on the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there was a building on the land
      `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building was fixed to the land and could lawfully be used as a place of residence
      `the building is suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building was suitable to live in (the Commissioner must also be of that opinion)
      `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone had lived in the home, or it had been sold as a place of residence, before your purchase
      `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home had been substantially renovated so that it counted as new residential premises for GST, with no one living in it or buying it as a home since
      `I am buying under the Help to Buy scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought under a Help to Buy arrangement with Housing Australia (answer no for purchases before 5 June 2026)
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years on the day of the transfer
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were under 18: whether the Commissioner exempted you from the age requirement
      `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were an Australian citizen or permanent resident
      `I or my spouse have owned a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse had owned a home anywhere in Australia before
      `I or my spouse have been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse had been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant before
      `I or my spouse got the 2018-2024 half-duty first home buyer concession before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to you or your spouse got this concession
      `I or my spouse got the first home buyer duty exemption before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to you or your spouse was exempt as a first home buyer (this does not bar the Division 2A concession)
      `I intend to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you intended to live in the home as your principal place of residence for 6 continuous months starting within 12 months
      `I am buying with one other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought the home with one other individual
      `the other buyer's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The other buyer's age in years on the day of the transfer
      `the Commissioner has exempted the other buyer from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the other buyer was under 18: whether the Commissioner exempted them
      `the other buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other buyer was an Australian citizen or permanent resident
      `the other buyer or their spouse has owned a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other buyer or their spouse had owned a home before
      `the other buyer or their spouse has been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other buyer or their spouse had been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant
      `the other buyer or their spouse got the 2018-2024 half-duty concession before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to the other buyer or their spouse got this concession
      `the other buyer or their spouse got the first home buyer duty exemption before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to the other buyer or their spouse was exempt as a first home buyer
      `the other buyer intends to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other buyer intended to live there for 6 continuous months starting within 12 months
      `the Commissioner accepts good reasons why a buyer who is not a first home buyer should not stop the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner was satisfied there were good reasons why a buyer who was not an eligible first home buyer should not prevent the concession (s 46D(2))
GIVETH A `First home buyer answer`
DECIDE `Did my home transfer get the 2018-2024 first home buyer concession` IS
    -- the first home buyer test reads neither the former home nor the foreign and Division 2C facts: fixed placeholders
    -- (no former home; FALSE, FALSE and a 1 January 2000 agreement day)
    `the first home buyer test under` `the first home buyer duty concession (Part 5 Division 2A)` `the settings in the deposited text`
        (`the transfer from my answers` `the day the land is transferred to me` `the price I pay` `what the property was worth when I signed the contract` `there is a building on the land` (`the building from my answers` `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` `the building is suitable to live in` `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since`)
            (`the transferees from my answers` (`an individual buyer` `my age` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `I or my spouse have owned a home before` `I or my spouse have been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant` `I or my spouse got the 2018-2024 half-duty first home buyer concession before` `I or my spouse got the first home buyer duty exemption before` `I intend to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months`) `I am buying with one other person` (`an individual buyer` `the other buyer's age` `the Commissioner has exempted the other buyer from the age requirement` `the other buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `the other buyer or their spouse has owned a home before` `the other buyer or their spouse has been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant` `the other buyer or their spouse got the 2018-2024 half-duty concession before` `the other buyer or their spouse got the first home buyer duty exemption before` `the other buyer intends to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months`) `I am buying under the Help to Buy scheme`)
            `no former home` `the Commissioner accepts good reasons why a buyer who is not a first home buyer should not stop the exemption` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1))

§§ `The pensioner duty concession (Part 5 Division 2B) -- a pensioner selling one home and buying another`

-- 22 answers, in this order: the transfer (9), my age and intention (2), my cards and earlier concession (4), my former
-- home (7). The buyer asking is the pensioner. The first home buyer fields of the pensioner's record (age exemption,
-- citizenship, earlier home, grant, Division 2A, Part 6 Division 2) are not read by the s 46L-46O test: fixed
-- placeholders. Buying alone, so the other-buyer record is a placeholder too, as are the good-reasons, foreign and
-- Division 2C facts at the end (FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1 January 2000), which the test does not read.
@export I am a pensioner selling my Tasmanian home and buying a cheaper one: is the duty on the new home halved under the pensioner duty concession (Duties Act 2001 Part 5 Division 2B, ss 46J-46O; the former home must be sold by 30 June 2025 as deposited)?
GIVEN `the day the land is transferred to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the new home's land is transferred to you (usually settlement)
      `the price I pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you pay for the new home, in Australian dollars, including any debt you take over
      `what the property was worth when I signed the contract` IS A NUMBER @desc What the new home could reasonably have been sold for on the open market when the contract was signed, free of any mortgage, in dollars
      `there is a building on the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a building on the land
      `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be used as a place of residence
      `the building is suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is suitable to live in (the Commissioner must also be of that opinion)
      `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone has lived in the home, or it has been sold as a home, before (the concession applies to new and established homes alike)
      `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home was substantially renovated so that it counts as new residential premises for GST, with no one living in it or buying it since
      `I am buying under the Help to Buy scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying under a Help to Buy arrangement with Housing Australia
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years on the day of the transfer
      `I intend to live in the new home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you intend to live in the new home as your principal place of residence for at least 6 continuous months starting within 12 months after the transfer (the Commissioner must be satisfied of this)
      `I hold a Pensioner Concession Card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a Pensioner Concession Card under a Commonwealth Act (Social Security Act 1991 or Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986)
      `I hold a Commonwealth Seniors Health Card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a Commonwealth Seniors Health Card (Social Security Act 1991)
      `I receive a special rate pension from Veterans' Affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a special rate pension under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986
      `I or my spouse got the pensioner duty concession before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to you or your spouse got the pensioner duty concession
      `I am selling a home in Tasmania that I lived in as my main home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are selling (or have sold) land in Tasmania with a home on it that you lived in as your principal place of residence
      `the day my former home is or was transferred` IS A DATE @desc The day your former home was, or will be, transferred to its buyer (usually settlement)
      `the dutiable value of my former home` IS A NUMBER @desc The dutiable value of your former home when it was transferred: the greater of its sale price and its market value, in dollars
      `I lived in my former home for the 6 months before selling it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your former home was your principal place of residence for the whole 6 months before you transferred it (or a shorter period the Commissioner approved)
      `I lived in my former home for the 6 months before buying the new home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your former home was your principal place of residence for the whole 6 months before the new home was transferred to you (counts only if you sell after buying)
      `the new home is in the same names as my former home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new home is owned in the same name or names as the former home was (or the Commissioner is satisfied there are good reasons why not)
      `I or my spouse owned another home when I bought the new home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse owned any other home in Australia (apart from the former home and the new one) when the new home was transferred to you
GIVETH A `Pensioner concession answer`
DECIDE `Is the duty on my new home halved under the pensioner concession` IS
    `the pensioner concession test` `the settings in the deposited text`
        (`the transfer from my answers` `the day the land is transferred to me` `the price I pay` `what the property was worth when I signed the contract` `there is a building on the land` (`the building from my answers` `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` `the building is suitable to live in` `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since`)
            (`the transferees from my answers` (`with the pensioner facts` (`an individual buyer` `my age` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `I intend to live in the new home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months`) `I hold a Pensioner Concession Card` `I hold a Commonwealth Seniors Health Card` `I receive a special rate pension from Veterans' Affairs` `I or my spouse got the pensioner duty concession before`) FALSE `Housing Australia under Help to Buy` `I am buying under the Help to Buy scheme`)
            (`the former home from my answers` `I am selling a home in Tasmania that I lived in as my main home` `the day my former home is or was transferred` `the dutiable value of my former home` `I lived in my former home for the 6 months before selling it` `I lived in my former home for the 6 months before buying the new home` `the new home is in the same names as my former home` `I or my spouse owned another home when I bought the new home`)
            FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1))

§§ `What transfer duty must I pay on my home`

-- 40 answers, in this order: the transfer (9), me (8), the other buyer (9), the Commissioner's good reasons (1), my
-- pensioner facts (4), my former home (7), the Division 2C facts (2). Whether a buyer is a foreign person is worked out
-- in the core from the citizenship answers (s 3 "foreign natural person"); the seat's buyers are individuals, so the
-- core's foreign corporation or trustee fact is a fixed FALSE.
@export What transfer duty must I pay on my Tasmanian home, transferred on this date, after the first home buyer exemption, the 2018-2024 first home buyer concession or the pensioner concession (Duties Act 2001 ss 29, 46E, 46N, 46O, 57G)?
GIVEN `the day the land is transferred to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the land is transferred to you (usually settlement)
      `the price I pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you pay, in Australian dollars, including any debt or mortgage you take over; under Help to Buy, the full price including the Commonwealth's contribution
      `what the property was worth when I signed the contract` IS A NUMBER @desc What the property could reasonably have been sold for on the open market when the contract was signed, free of any mortgage, in dollars
      `there is a building on the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a building on the land (answer no for vacant land)
      `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be used as a place of residence
      `the building is suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building is suitable to live in (the Commissioner must also be of that opinion)
      `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone has lived in the home, or it has been sold as a place of residence, before your purchase
      `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home was substantially renovated so that it counts as new residential premises for GST, with no one living in it or buying it since
      `I am buying under the Help to Buy scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying under a Help to Buy arrangement with Housing Australia
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years on the day of the transfer
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are under 18: whether the Commissioner has exempted you from the age requirement
      `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, the holder of a permanent visa, or a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa
      `I or my spouse have owned a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse (even if separated) have ever owned a home anywhere in Australia, whether or not you lived there
      `I or my spouse have been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse have ever been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant, even if it was paid back
      `I or my spouse got the 2018-2024 half-duty first home buyer concession before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to you or your spouse got the Division 2A first home buyer duty concession
      `I or my spouse got the first home buyer duty exemption before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to you or your spouse was exempt from duty as a first home buyer
      `I intend to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you intend to live in the home as your principal place of residence for at least 6 continuous months starting within 12 months after the transfer
      `I am buying with one other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying the home with one other individual (not counting Housing Australia under Help to Buy)
      `the other buyer's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The other buyer's age in years on the day of the transfer
      `the Commissioner has exempted the other buyer from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the other buyer is under 18: whether the Commissioner has exempted them
      `the other buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident
      `the other buyer or their spouse has owned a home before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other buyer or their spouse has ever owned a home anywhere in Australia
      `the other buyer or their spouse has been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other buyer or their spouse has ever been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant
      `the other buyer or their spouse got the 2018-2024 half-duty concession before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to the other buyer or their spouse got the Division 2A concession
      `the other buyer or their spouse got the first home buyer duty exemption before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to the other buyer or their spouse was exempt as a first home buyer
      `the other buyer intends to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other buyer intends to live there for 6 continuous months starting within 12 months
      `the Commissioner accepts good reasons why a buyer who is not a first home buyer should not stop the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied there are good reasons why a buyer who is not an eligible first home buyer should not prevent the exemption or concession; answer no unless the Commissioner has said so
      `I hold a Pensioner Concession Card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a Pensioner Concession Card under a Commonwealth Act
      `I hold a Commonwealth Seniors Health Card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a Commonwealth Seniors Health Card
      `I receive a special rate pension from Veterans' Affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive a special rate pension under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986
      `I or my spouse got the pensioner duty concession before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an earlier transfer to you or your spouse got the pensioner duty concession
      `I am selling a home in Tasmania that I lived in as my main home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are selling (or have sold) land in Tasmania with a home on it that you lived in as your principal place of residence
      `the day my former home is or was transferred` IS A DATE @desc The day your former home was, or will be, transferred to its buyer
      `the dutiable value of my former home` IS A NUMBER @desc The dutiable value of your former home when transferred: the greater of its sale price and market value, in dollars
      `I lived in my former home for the 6 months before selling it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your former home was your principal place of residence for the 6 months before you transferred it (or a shorter period the Commissioner approved)
      `I lived in my former home for the 6 months before buying the new home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your former home was your principal place of residence for the 6 months before the new home was transferred to you
      `the new home is in the same names as my former home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new home is owned in the same name or names as the former home (or the Commissioner is satisfied of good reasons why not)
      `I or my spouse owned another home when I bought the new home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse owned any other home in Australia (apart from the former and new homes) when the new home was transferred
      `the home is a strata lot or shares a wall, and its occupancy permit had not been granted when I signed the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is a strata lot, or a dwelling on its own title that shares a wall with another (or one the Commissioner has determined is eligible for the pre-completion concession), and its occupancy permit had not been granted when you signed the contract (bought off the plan)
      `the day I signed the contract` IS A DATE @desc The day you signed the contract (agreement for sale) to buy the home; it matters only for an off-the-plan strata or shared-wall home
GIVETH A `Transfer duty answer`
DECIDE `What transfer duty must I pay on my home` IS
    `the transfer duty on` `the settings in the deposited text`
        (`the transfer from my answers` `the day the land is transferred to me` `the price I pay` `what the property was worth when I signed the contract` `there is a building on the land` (`the building from my answers` `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` `the building is suitable to live in` `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since`)
            (`the transferees from my answers` (`with the pensioner facts` (`an individual buyer` `my age` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `I or my spouse have owned a home before` `I or my spouse have been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant` `I or my spouse got the 2018-2024 half-duty first home buyer concession before` `I or my spouse got the first home buyer duty exemption before` `I intend to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months`) `I hold a Pensioner Concession Card` `I hold a Commonwealth Seniors Health Card` `I receive a special rate pension from Veterans' Affairs` `I or my spouse got the pensioner duty concession before`) `I am buying with one other person` (`an individual buyer` `the other buyer's age` `the Commissioner has exempted the other buyer from the age requirement` `the other buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `the other buyer or their spouse has owned a home before` `the other buyer or their spouse has been paid a Tasmanian first home owner grant` `the other buyer or their spouse got the 2018-2024 half-duty concession before` `the other buyer or their spouse got the first home buyer duty exemption before` `the other buyer intends to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months`) `I am buying under the Help to Buy scheme`)
            (`the former home from my answers` `I am selling a home in Tasmania that I lived in as my main home` `the day my former home is or was transferred` `the dutiable value of my former home` `I lived in my former home for the 6 months before selling it` `I lived in my former home for the 6 months before buying the new home` `the new home is in the same names as my former home` `I or my spouse owned another home when I bought the new home`)
            `the Commissioner accepts good reasons why a buyer who is not a first home buyer should not stop the exemption`
            -- no foreign corporation or trustee among the buyers: the seat's buyers are individuals
            FALSE
            `the home is a strata lot or shares a wall, and its occupancy permit had not been granted when I signed the contract`
            `the day I signed the contract`)

@export By what date must I lodge my Tasmanian home transfer with the Commissioner and pay the duty (Duties Act 2001 ss 13-15: within 3 months after the transfer)?
GIVEN `the day the land is transferred to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the land is transferred to you (the day the liability for duty arises, s 10)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I lodge and pay the duty on my home` IS
    `the last day to lodge and pay` `the day the land is transferred to me`

§§ `After settlement: living in the home, for the duty exemption (s 57H) -- situation: the exemption was given`

DECLARE `Residence dates` HAS
    `I must move in no later than`                              IS A DATE
    `if I move in on the day I gave, I must stay and keep my interest until at least` IS A DATE

@export My home transfer was exempt as a first home buyer: by what date must I move in, and until what date must I keep living there and keep my interest (Duties Act 2001 s 57H)?
GIVEN `the day the land was transferred to me` IS A DATE @desc The day the land was transferred to you
      `the months the Commissioner allowed me to move in` IS A NUMBER @desc The months after the transfer within which you must start living there: 12, unless the Commissioner approved a longer period (s 57H(1)(b))
      `the months I must live there` IS A NUMBER @desc The months you must live there continuously: 6, unless the Commissioner approved a shorter period for good reasons (s 57H(2))
      `the day I moved in or will move in` IS A DATE @desc The day you started, or will start, living in the home as your principal place of residence
GIVETH A `Residence dates`
DECIDE `By when must I move in and how long must I stay, for the exemption` IS
    `Residence dates` WITH
        `I must move in no later than`                              IS `the day that is` `the months the Commissioner allowed me to move in` `months after` `the day the land was transferred to me`
        `if I move in on the day I gave, I must stay and keep my interest until at least` IS `the day that is` `the months I must live there` `months after` `the day I moved in or will move in`

DECLARE `Failure answer` HAS
    `I must give the Commissioner written notice no later than`  IS A DATE
    `the duty the Commissioner may then reassess, in dollars`   IS A NUMBER
    `the most I can be fined for not giving notice, in penalty units` IS A NUMBER

@export I did not move in, did not stay long enough, or sold or gave up my interest, after my home transfer was exempt as a first home buyer: by what date must I tell the Commissioner, and what duty can then be charged (Duties Act 2001 ss 57H(6), 57I)?
GIVEN `the day I failed the residence requirement` IS A DATE @desc The day of the failure: the day after the last day to move in passed, the day you stopped living there when it was too late to start a fresh 6 months, or the day you ceased to hold your interest in the land
      `the price I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you paid for the home, in Australian dollars
      `what the property was worth when I signed the contract` IS A NUMBER @desc What the property could reasonably have been sold for on the open market when the contract was signed, in dollars
GIVETH A `Failure answer`
DECIDE `What must I do after failing the residence requirement for the exemption` IS
    -- the reassessable duty reads only the price and the value: the transfer's other fields are fixed placeholders
    `Failure answer` WITH
        `I must give the Commissioner written notice no later than`  IS `the day that is` `the days to act after a failure of the residence requirement` `days after` `the day I failed the residence requirement`
        `the duty the Commissioner may then reassess, in dollars`   IS `the duty the Commissioner may reassess on a failure (ss 46G(2), 57I(2))` (`the transfer from my answers` `the day I failed the residence requirement` `the price I paid` `what the property was worth when I signed the contract` FALSE (`the building from my answers` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EMPTY `no former home` FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1))
        `the most I can be fined for not giving notice, in penalty units` IS `the most fine, in penalty units, for not acting after a failure under` `the first home buyer duty exemption (Duties Act s 57H)`

§§ `The first home owner grant (new homes) -- FHOG Act 2000`

-- One applicant's answers, built into the core's record.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `age exempted` IS A BOOLEAN, `citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `earlier grant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid back` IS A BOOLEAN, `before 2000` IS A BOOLEAN, `owned and lived` IS A BOOLEAN, `intends` IS A BOOLEAN
      `residence exempted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Grant applicant`
`a grant applicant` `age` `age exempted` `citizen` `earlier grant` `paid back` `before 2000` `owned and lived` `intends` `residence exempted` MEANS
    `Grant applicant` WITH
        `is a natural person`                                                                        IS TRUE
        `age`                                                                                        IS `age`
        `the Commissioner exempts the age requirement (s 8(2))`                                      IS `age exempted`
        `is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident`                                           IS `citizen`
        `the applicant or spouse was a party to an earlier application, under this Act or a corresponding law, on which a grant was paid` IS `earlier grant`
        `that earlier grant was paid back`                                                           IS `paid back`
        `the applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia before 1 July 2000` IS `before 2000`
        `the applicant or spouse, before the commencement date, held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia and occupied it as a residence for a continuous 6 months` IS `owned and lived`
        `intends to meet, or has met, the residence requirement`                                     IS `intends`
        `the Commissioner exempts the applicant from the residence requirement (s 12(2))`            IS `residence exempted`

GIVEN `me` IS A `Grant applicant`, `with another` IS A BOOLEAN, `the other` IS A `Grant applicant`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Grant applicant`
`the applicants from my answers` `me` `with another` `the other` MEANS
    IF `with another` THEN LIST `me`, `the other` ELSE LIST `me`

