@export Do I (and the person applying with me) meet the eligibility criteria for the Tasmanian first home owner grant (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 ss 8-12)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are under 18: whether the Commissioner has exempted you (s 8(2))
      `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen, the holder of a permanent visa, or a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa
      `I or my spouse were paid a first home owner grant before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse (husband, wife or significant-relationship partner; not a separated spouse) were party to an earlier application, in Tasmania or another State or Territory, on which a grant was paid
      `that earlier grant was paid back` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that earlier grant was later paid back
      `I or my spouse held an interest in a home in Australia before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse held a relevant interest (such as freehold) in residential property anywhere in Australia before 1 July 2000
      `I or my spouse have owned a home in Australia and lived in it for 6 months in a row` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your spouse, before the contract or start of building, held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia and lived in it for at least 6 continuous months
      `I intend to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months of completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you intend to live in (or have lived in) the home as your principal place of residence for 6 continuous months, starting within 12 months after completion
      `the Commissioner has exempted me from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a joint applicant only: whether the Commissioner has exempted you from living there because the other applicant does (s 12(2))
      `I am applying with one other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one other person is applying for the grant with you (everyone who will own the home must apply)
      `the other applicant's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The other applicant's age in years
      `the Commissioner has exempted the other applicant from the age requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the other applicant is under 18: whether the Commissioner has exempted them
      `the other applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident
      `the other applicant or their spouse were paid a first home owner grant before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other applicant or their spouse were party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid
      `the other applicant's earlier grant was paid back` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that earlier grant was paid back
      `the other applicant or their spouse held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other applicant or their spouse held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia before 1 July 2000
      `the other applicant or their spouse have owned a home and lived in it for 6 months in a row` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other applicant or their spouse held a relevant interest in residential property in Australia and lived in it for 6 continuous months
      `the other applicant intends to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other applicant intends to live in the home for 6 continuous months starting within 12 months after completion
      `the Commissioner has exempted the other applicant from the residence requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has exempted the other applicant from living there because you do
GIVETH A MAYBE `Criterion not met`
DECIDE `Do we meet the grant's eligibility criteria` IS
    `the eligibility criteria not met by`
        (`the applicants from my answers`
            (`a grant applicant` `my age` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the age requirement` `I am an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `I or my spouse were paid a first home owner grant before` `that earlier grant was paid back` `I or my spouse held an interest in a home in Australia before 1 July 2000` `I or my spouse have owned a home in Australia and lived in it for 6 months in a row` `I intend to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months of completion` `the Commissioner has exempted me from the residence requirement`)
            `I am applying with one other person`
            (`a grant applicant` `the other applicant's age` `the Commissioner has exempted the other applicant from the age requirement` `the other applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `the other applicant or their spouse were paid a first home owner grant before` `the other applicant's earlier grant was paid back` `the other applicant or their spouse held an interest in a home before 1 July 2000` `the other applicant or their spouse have owned a home and lived in it for 6 months in a row` `the other applicant intends to live in the home for 6 months in a row, starting within 12 months` `the Commissioner has exempted the other applicant from the residence requirement`))

@export Is my contract to buy a home, my building contract, or my owner-builder build an eligible transaction for the Tasmanian first home owner grant (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 s 13)?
GIVEN `what I am doing` IS A `Grant transaction kind` @desc One of: a contract to buy a home; a comprehensive home building contract (a builder builds the whole home); building the home as an owner builder; buying a moveable building to put on my land
      `the home is in Tasmania` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is in Tasmania
      `the commencement date` IS A DATE @desc The day the contract was made, or for an owner builder the day laying the foundations began
      `I am or will be the owner of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a building contract: whether you own the land, or will own it on completion of the contract
      `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is (or will be) fixed to the land and may lawfully be used as a place of residence
      `the building is suitable to live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is (or will be) suitable to live in (the Commissioner must also be of that opinion)
      `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a purchase: whether anyone has lived in the home, or it has been sold as a home, before your contract
      `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a purchase: whether the home was substantially renovated so that it counts as new residential premises for GST, with no one living in it or buying it since
      `the Commissioner thinks it is part of a scheme to get around the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is of the opinion that the transaction is part of a scheme to get around the Act's limits (s 13(3)); answer no unless told so
GIVETH A `Transaction answer`
DECIDE `Is my transaction eligible for the grant` IS
    -- completion date, completion, price and the s 7(4), s 46X(2) and s 18 facts are not read by s 13: fixed placeholders
    `the s 13 test for`
        (`the grant transaction from my answers` `what I am doing` `the home is in Tasmania` `the commencement date` `the commencement date` FALSE 0 `I am or will be the owner of the land` (`the building from my answers` `the building is fixed to the land and may lawfully be lived in` `the building is suitable to live in` `someone has lived in it, or it has been sold as a home, before` `it was substantially renovated and no one has lived in it or bought it as a home since`) `the Commissioner thinks it is part of a scheme to get around the Act` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

