§§ `After completion: living in the home, for a grant paid in anticipation (FHOG Act ss 12, 20) -- situation: the grant was paid before the residence requirement was met`

@export My first home owner grant was paid before I moved in: by what date must I move in, and until what date must I keep living there and keep my interest (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 ss 12, 20)?
GIVEN `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The day the purchase settled or the home was ready to live in
      `the months the Commissioner allowed me to move in` IS A NUMBER @desc The months after completion within which you must start living there: 12, unless the Commissioner approved a longer period
      `the months I must live there` IS A NUMBER @desc The months you must live there continuously: 6, unless the Commissioner approved a shorter period for good reasons (s 12(1A))
      `the day I moved in or will move in` IS A DATE @desc The day you started, or will start, living in the home as your principal place of residence
GIVETH A `Residence dates`
DECIDE `By when must I move in and how long must I stay, for the grant` IS
    `Residence dates` WITH
        `I must move in no later than`                              IS `the day that is` `the months the Commissioner allowed me to move in` `months after` `the completion date`
        `if I move in on the day I gave, I must stay and keep my interest until at least` IS `the day that is` `the months I must live there` `months after` `the day I moved in or will move in`

DECLARE `Grant repayment answer` HAS
    `I must tell the Commissioner in writing and repay the grant no later than` IS A DATE
    `the most I can be fined, in penalty units`                                 IS A NUMBER

@export My first home owner grant was paid before I moved in, and I will not (or did not) meet the residence requirement: by what date must I tell the Commissioner and repay the grant (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 s 20(2)-(4))?
