    `the most penalty that can be imposed (s 38(3))` `the amount I must repay`

§ `Registering a motor vehicle in Tasmania`

§§ `Duties Act 2001 Chapter 8 -- vehicle duty`

GIVEN `day` IS A DATE, `dealing` IS A `Vehicle dealing`, `heavy` IS A BOOLEAN, `motor cycle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for passengers` IS A BOOLEAN, `off-road or truck chassis` IS A BOOLEAN, `ute` IS A BOOLEAN, `more than 9 seats` IS A BOOLEAN
      `new` IS A BOOLEAN, `fleet discount` IS A BOOLEAN, `price` IS A NUMBER, `market value` IS A NUMBER
      `adequate` IS A BOOLEAN, `exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Vehicle facts`
`the vehicle from my answers` `day` `dealing` `heavy` `motor cycle` `for passengers` `off-road or truck chassis` `ute` `more than 9 seats` `new` `fleet discount` `price` `market value` `adequate` `exemption` MEANS
    `Vehicle facts` WITH
        `the day of the application`                                                             IS `day`
        `the dealing`                                                                            IS `dealing`
        `is a heavy vehicle (Heavy Vehicle National Law, not a camper van)`                      IS `heavy`
        `is a motor cycle`                                                                       IS `motor cycle`
        `is constructed principally for the carriage of passengers`                              IS `for passengers`
        `is designed for not more than 9 adults and built on a truck chassis or with off-road features` IS `off-road or truck chassis`
        `has a utility or panel van body whose forward part and mechanics are those of the maker's passenger vehicle` IS `ute`
        `is equipped to seat more than 9 adults, including the driver`                           IS `more than 9 seats`
        `is a new motor vehicle`                                                                 IS `new`
        `the manufacturer gave the purchaser a discount off the normal retail price not available to the general public` IS `fleet discount`
        `the consideration`                                                                      IS `price`
        `the market value`                                                                       IS `market value`
        `the Commissioner is satisfied the consideration is adequate for the value of the new vehicle (s 198(1A))` IS `adequate`
        `an exemption under ss 199 to 203 is claimed`                                            IS `exemption`

@export Is duty charged on my motor vehicle application or notice in Tasmania, and who pays it (Duties Act 2001 ss 192, 195)?
GIVEN `what I am lodging` IS A `Vehicle dealing` @desc One of: an application to register a vehicle not previously registered under the Vehicle and Traffic Act 1999; an application to register a vehicle in a name different from its last registration; a notice of a change of beneficial ownership; an application to register a vehicle in the same name or names as its last registration
GIVETH A `Vehicle duty payer`
DECIDE `Who pays duty on my vehicle application` IS
    `who pays the vehicle duty (s 195)` `what I am lodging`

-- 14 answers, in this order: the day, the dealing, the kind of vehicle (6), new and fleet discount (2), the price and
-- market value (2), the Commissioner's satisfaction (1), an exemption claimed (1).
@export How much duty must I pay to register my motor vehicle in Tasmania, or on a change of its ownership (Duties Act 2001 ss 192, 197, 198: $3 per $100 or part; passenger vehicles $1,050 plus $11 per $100 over $35,000 up to $40,000, then $4 per $100 of the whole value; $20 at $600 or less)?
GIVEN `the day of my application` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply to register the vehicle or give the notice of change of beneficial ownership
      `what I am lodging` IS A `Vehicle dealing` @desc One of: an application to register a vehicle not previously registered under the Vehicle and Traffic Act 1999; an application to register a vehicle in a name different from its last registration; a notice of a change of beneficial ownership; an application to register a vehicle in the same name or names as its last registration
      `it is a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a heavy vehicle under the Heavy Vehicle National Law (over 4.5 tonnes gross vehicle mass), other than a camper van
      `it is a motor cycle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a motor cycle
      `it is built mainly to carry passengers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is constructed principally for the carriage of passengers (cars, station wagons, people movers)
      `it seats up to 9 adults and is built on a truck chassis or for off-road use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is designed principally to carry not more than 9 adults including the driver, and is built on a truck chassis or with special features for off-road operation (most four-wheel drives)
      `it is a ute or panel van built on the maker's passenger car` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has a utility or panel van body whose front and most of whose mechanical equipment are those of a passenger vehicle made by the same manufacturer
      `it seats more than 9 adults` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is built to carry passengers and equipped to seat more than 9 adults including the driver
      `it is a new vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a new motor vehicle
      `the manufacturer gave me a fleet discount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the manufacturer gave you a discount off the normal retail price that is not available to the general public (a manufacturer's fleet discount)
      `the price I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you paid for the vehicle, in money or money's worth, in dollars, leaving out any extended warranty premium and equipment moved from your other vehicle
      `its market value` IS A NUMBER @desc What the vehicle might reasonably sell for on the open market, free of encumbrances, in dollars (at acquisition for a used vehicle, otherwise when you apply)
      `the price is accepted as adequate for a new vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a new vehicle: whether the Commissioner is satisfied that the price is adequate for its value (then the price alone is the dutiable value)
      `I claim an exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim an exemption or refund under ss 199-203 (deceased estate, family law property settlement, financier's repossession, motor-tax-exempt vehicle, duty paid in another State, and others) -- not covered here
GIVETH A `Vehicle duty answer`
DECIDE `How much duty must I pay to register my vehicle` IS
    `the vehicle duty on` (`the vehicle from my answers` `the day of my application` `what I am lodging` `it is a heavy vehicle` `it is a motor cycle` `it is built mainly to carry passengers` `it seats up to 9 adults and is built on a truck chassis or for off-road use` `it is a ute or panel van built on the maker's passenger car` `it seats more than 9 adults` `it is a new vehicle` `the manufacturer gave me a fleet discount` `the price I paid` `its market value` `the price is accepted as adequate for a new vehicle` `I claim an exemption`)

@export What is the dutiable value of my motor vehicle for Tasmanian vehicle duty: the greater of the price and the market value, or the price alone for a new vehicle the Commissioner accepts (Duties Act 2001 s 198)?
GIVEN `it is a new vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a new motor vehicle
      `the price I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you paid, in money or money's worth, in dollars, leaving out any extended warranty premium
      `its market value` IS A NUMBER @desc What the vehicle might reasonably sell for on the open market, free of encumbrances, in dollars
      `the price is accepted as adequate for a new vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a new vehicle: whether the Commissioner is satisfied that the price is adequate for its value
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the dutiable value of my vehicle` IS
    -- s 198 reads only these four facts: the others are fixed placeholders
    `the dutiable value of the vehicle (s 198)` (`the vehicle from my answers` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) `an application to register a vehicle not previously registered under the Vehicle and Traffic Act 1999` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `it is a new vehicle` FALSE `the price I paid` `its market value` `the price is accepted as adequate for a new vehicle` FALSE)

@export Must I lodge a statement of my vehicle's dutiable value with my application, on pain of a fine of up to 100 penalty units (Duties Act 2001 s 193(1))?
GIVEN `what I am lodging` IS A `Vehicle dealing` @desc One of: an application to register a vehicle not previously registered; an application to register in a name different from the last registration; a notice of a change of beneficial ownership; an application to register in the same name or names
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I lodge a statement of the dutiable value` IF
    `is charged with duty (s 192)` `what I am lodging`
